systemic_fix:
Same fix J571BH specified on 2026-08-28, now overdue across 5 cycles (08-28 through 09-01) of confirmed active recurrence: in systems/dream-cycle/salience-score.py's update_salience_block(), the regex `r"
salience:\s*
(?:[ 	]+[^
]*
)*"` requires every indented line of the old salience: block to end in a literal newline -- but because fm_section = content[3:end] excludes the newline immediately before the closing '
---' delimiter, the block's last line never has one, so it survives the sub() untouched and gets stranded. One-line fix: change the trailing repetition group to `(?:[ 	]+[^
]*
?)*` (optional trailing newline) so the last line is consumed too. Separately, parse_frontmatter()'s promoted_m = re.search(...) takes the FIRST regex match scanning top-down, which is backwards for a corpus where orphans accumulate above the authoritative last block -- should scan for the LAST match, not the first, once the stranding fix stops adding new orphans. Recommend Rigby apply both in the same patch and re-run this cycle's repair script's validation query (yaml.safe_load over all episodic files) as its acceptance test.
